---
/**
 * Yolk Post's terms and conditions (the Android game). Linked from Google Play and from the game.
 * Facts come from build 1.0.0: World 1 free; one optional one-time purchase (the full route) opens every
 * other world, including later ones, and removes between-delivery ads (ADR-0011, ADR-0012); a grown-up
 * check before buying; rewarded videos optional; stamps, parcels and wardrobe items earned only; progress
 * saved only on the device; the purchase is restored through Google Play.
 */
import LegalLayout from '../../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../../lib/site';

const toc = [
  { id: 'game', label: 'The game' },
  { id: 'route', label: 'The full route purchase' },
  { id: 'refunds', label: 'Refunds' },
  { id: 'ads', label: 'Ads and reward videos' },
  { id: 'items', label: 'Stamps, parcels and outfits' },
  { id: 'progress', label: 'Your progress' },
  { id: 'fair', label: 'Fair play' },
  { id: 'ours', label: 'What is ours' },
  { id: 'warranty', label: 'No guarantee' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Yolk Post terms and conditions"
  description="The rules for playing Yolk Post, the platform game for Android by IsmailApps: World 1 free, one optional purchase for the full route, child-safe ads, progress saved on your phone."
  updated="21 November 2026"
  toc={toc}
  crumbs={[
    { href: '/', label: 'Home' },
    { href: '/games', label: 'Games' },
    { href: '/games/yolk-post', label: 'Yolk Post' },
    { label: 'Terms and conditions' },
  ]}
>
  <p>
    These terms apply when you download or play <strong>Yolk Post</strong>, our platform game for Android. By playing, you
    agree to them. If you are under 18, please read them with a parent or guardian, and ask them before buying anything. How
    the game handles data is explained in the <a href="/games/yolk-post/privacy-policy">Yolk Post privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="game">The game</h2>
  <p>
    Yolk Post is free to download, and World 1 is free to play in full. It is made by IsmailApps ({site.founder.legalName}).
    You may play it for your own personal, non-commercial enjoyment. Google Play's own terms also apply to downloading it and
    to buying anything in it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="route">The full route purchase</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      The game sells <strong>one thing</strong>: the full route, a one-time purchase. It opens every world after World 1,
      including any worlds we add to the game later, and removes the ads between deliveries.
    </li>
    <li>It is not a subscription. You pay once, at the price Google Play shows you before you confirm.</li>
    <li>A grown-up check (a times-table question) comes before the purchase screen.</li>
    <li>
      The purchase belongs to the Google account you bought it with. On a new phone or after reinstalling, sign in to Google
      Play with that account and tap <strong>Restore purchase</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>There are no coins, gems, loot boxes or other purchases in the game.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="refunds">Refunds</h2>
  <p>
    Purchases are handled by Google Play, so Google Play's
    <a href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/answer/2479637" rel="noopener">refund policy</a> applies. You can usually
    ask Google for a refund within 48 hours of buying. After that, or if something went wrong, email us at
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with your Google Play order number and we will help. Nothing here limits
    your rights under consumer law.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ads">Ads and reward videos</h2>
  <p>
    In the free version, short ads can appear between some deliveries, never during play. Some extras, such as skipping a
    delivery you are stuck on, come from a short video that you choose to watch. A reward is given only when Google's ad
    service confirms the video was watched; closing it early gives nothing. Videos are not always available. Ads are shown by
    Google AdMob. We don't choose which advertiser appears, but we only allow ads rated for general audiences.
  </p>

  <h2 id="items">Stamps, parcels and outfits</h2>
  <p>
    Stamps, lost parcels, badges, caps and plasters are parts of the game. They are <strong>earned only by playing</strong>,
    are never sold, have no real-money value, are not your property, and cannot be exchanged for money or anything outside
    the game.
  </p>

  <h2 id="progress">Your progress</h2>
  <p>
    Your progress is saved only on your phone. If you uninstall the game, clear its data or change phones, it is gone, and we
    cannot restore it, because we never had a copy. Your full route purchase is the exception: Google Play keeps it with your
    account, so you can restore it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="fair">Fair play</h2>
  <p>
    Please don't modify the game, its files or its save data to unlock worlds or rewards you haven't earned or bought. We may
    correct this in a later update.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ours">What is ours</h2>
  <p>
    The game, its levels, story, characters (including Gus and Shelly), pictures, music and sounds belong to IsmailApps or are
    used under licence. You may share screenshots and videos of your own play. Please don't copy, resell or redistribute the
    game itself.
  </p>

  <h2 id="warranty">No guarantee</h2>
  <p>
    We work hard to make Yolk Post fun and free of bugs, but the game is provided "as is", without a promise that it will
    always work, be available, or suit every device. As far as the law allows, we are not liable for any loss caused by using
    the game, including lost progress. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under consumer law that cannot be
    limited, including your rights over something you paid for.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update the game and these terms. When the terms change, we update the date at the top of this page. If you keep
    playing after that, the new terms apply. A change will never take away a full route you already bought.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions, problems or ideas: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
